nodes.statement:
Consider a bimodal density $f$ in $\mathbb{R}^d$ with modes at $\pm \mu$. Under the rescaling $Y = cX$, the transformed density $f_Y$ has modes at $\pm c\mu$. With $A_0 = I_d$, the canonical SDE for $X$ is $dX_t =  rac{1}{2}
abla \log f(X_t)\,dt + dW_t$, while for $Y$ it is $dY_t =  rac{1}{2}
abla \log f_Y(Y_t)\,dt + dW_t$. The drift scales as $
abla_y \log f_Y(y) =  rac{1}{c}
abla_x \log f(x)$, so the drift-to-diffusion ratio changes by a factor of $1/c$: stretching the space ($c > 1$) weakens the drift relative to the noise, making the process mix faster and lowering SSA, even though the distribution has the same shape. The multimodality measure would depend on the choice of units rather than on the geometry of~$f$.
